scenario_text:
**PagerDuty — Incident #PD-4471 (Triggered: Jun 14, 2026, 02:17 AM)**
Service: auth-service | Severity: SEV-1
Alert: 'Bulk export of user records from tenant: Covington Medical Group'
Escalation: On-call (Jordan Kim) ack'd 02:19 → Security on-call (Priya Venkatesh) paged 02:25

**Slack — #incidents (Jun 14, 2026, 02:32 AM)**
@jordan.kim: Confirmed unauthorized access to Covington tenant. Compromised API key exported ~12K user records (names, emails, hashed passwords). Key rotated 02:28. Blast radius contained to single tenant.
@priya.v: Activating breach response. @legal-oncall who's up?
@sarah.legal: Here. Which customer?
@priya.v: Covington Medical Group — healthcare customer. BAA in place?

**Google Drive — /Legal/DPAs/Executed/ (search results)**
- Covington_Medical_DPA_2024.pdf — Section 7: 'Processor shall notify Controller within 72 hours of becoming aware of a Personal Data Breach.'
- Covington_Medical_BAA_2023.pdf — Section 4.1: 'Business Associate shall notify Covered Entity of a Breach of Unsecured PHI within 24 hours of discovery.'

**Slack — #incidents thread (Jun 14, 2026, 02:48 AM)**
@sarah.legal: Both a DPA (72hr) and BAA (24hr) with Covington. BAA governs for data qualifying as PHI.
@priya.v: Exported data is names + emails + hashed passwords. No diagnosis codes. Is that PHI?
@sarah.legal: Patient-facing portal users at a medical practice — the fact someone HAS an account is itself health information. Arguably yes.
@priya.v: So we're on 24hr clock starting when?
@sarah.legal: Discovery = confirmed unauthorized access. 02:32 AM per Jordan's message. Deadline: 02:32 AM Jun 15.
[Thread: 4 :eyes: reactions, no further replies]

**Confluence — Incident Response Playbook: Data Breach (v2.1, Nov 2025)**
Section 6.2: 'For breaches affecting 500+ records, VP Engineering AND General Counsel must jointly approve notification content before delivery.'

**Jira — SEC-1201 (Created: Jun 14, 2026, 03:15 AM)**
Summary: Covington Medical breach notification — 24hr BAA deadline
Status: In Progress | Priority: Critical
Comment (@priya.v, 03:20 AM): 'Drafted notification. Need VP Eng + GC sign-off per s6.2 (12K > 500 threshold). @vp.eng @gc.martinez — deadline 02:32 AM Jun 15.'
Comment (@gc.martinez, 07:45 AM): 'Are we certain this is PHI? If just portal credentials, may not meet PHI definition. If not PHI, 72hr DPA clock applies instead.'

**Slack — DM between @priya.v and @sarah.legal (Jun 14, 2026, 08:15 AM)**
@priya.v: GC pushing back on PHI determination. I'd rather over-notify. Missing BAA deadline if it IS PHI = HIPAA violation.
@sarah.legal: Agree. But playbook says GC must approve content. Can't send without her sign-off.
@priya.v: Can VP Eng approve solo and I send with 'GC review pending' note?
@sarah.legal: That's not what s6.2 says. It says 'jointly approve.' :no_entry_sign:
